     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Im not sure how to handle operations that come before the actual deletion of the file via akubra:",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Should the operation prior to the file deletion execute normally (e.g. ResourceIndex deletion) and as soon as fedora hits an inexistant file return a 500 or should  fedora check if all the binary data exists it it supposed to delete before any other operations?",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
