       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0a085860c80a2aebafcf45ba3b2c30fc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFA-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0a085860c80a2aebafcf45ba3b2c30fc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFA-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0a085860c80a2aebafcf45ba3b2c30fc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFA-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "frank asseg",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a48a5426330072ea6384",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Hmm we have a problem here, since these are all handled via BaseRestResource.handleException():160",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "and ObjectNotInLowLevelStorageExceptions are mapped to a 404. changing this to a 500 will possibly impact other parts of the REST Api.",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "As it is now, a 404 would be returned if a nonexistant datastream is purged.",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "How to go on here? Should i introduce logic to differ between datastreams and objects so that for one a 404 can be returned while the other one returns a 500?",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "or leave it like this?",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
