  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Errors in the ILowLevelStorage are not correctly reported.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "A couple of examples:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "A) Managed content datastream file missing",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "create an object",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "add a managed content datastream",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "locate in the Akubra datastream store",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "delete the file",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "do a REST API delete",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "result: 200 reported, WARN in the log file.  This I think should be a 500 and an ERROR (or even FAIL)",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "B) FOXML file missing",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "create an object",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "locate the FOXML file in the Akubra object store",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "delete the file",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "do a REST API delete",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "result: 404 reported, WARN in the log file.  Again I think this should be a 500 and an ERROR or FAIL",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Suggest implementation of some test cases for this based on \"wrapping\" the Akubra implementation in such a way that exceptions can be configurably forced (eg pass parameter to the storage layer that specifies \"throw an exception if trying to read object ns:pid/dsid\") then test various API methods to ensure that 500 errors are reported (and ERROR/FAIL logged) when there has been a failure in the storage layer.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
