      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Im not sure how to handle operations that come before the actual deletion of the file via akubra:<br/>\nShould the operation prior to the file deletion execute normally (e.g. ResourceIndex deletion) and as soon as fedora hits an inexistant file return a 500 or should  fedora check if all the binary data exists it it supposed to delete before any other operations?</p>",
