  "description": "<p>Errors in the ILowLevelStorage are not correctly reported.</p>\n\n<p>A couple of examples:</p>\n\n<p>A) Managed content datastream file missing</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>create an object</li>\n\t<li>add a managed content datastream</li>\n\t<li>locate in the Akubra datastream store</li>\n\t<li>delete the file</li>\n\t<li>do a REST API delete<br/>\nresult: 200 reported, WARN in the log file.  This I think should be a 500 and an ERROR (or even FAIL)</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>B) FOXML file missing</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>create an object</li>\n\t<li>locate the FOXML file in the Akubra object store</li>\n\t<li>delete the file</li>\n\t<li>do a REST API delete<br/>\nresult: 404 reported, WARN in the log file.  Again I think this should be a 500 and an ERROR or FAIL</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>Suggest implementation of some test cases for this based on \"wrapping\" the Akubra implementation in such a way that exceptions can be configurably forced (eg pass parameter to the storage layer that specifies \"throw an exception if trying to read object ns:pid/dsid\") then test various API methods to ensure that 500 errors are reported (and ERROR/FAIL logged) when there has been a failure in the storage layer.</p>\n",
